Draw the framebuffer console at 4x instead of 2x so the kernel's own console
(including the SWEET sampler's pc/lr/bt hex and CRASH reports) can be read off
a 1080p photo of the panel.

The onclite has no usable UART; FBCON_SCALE 2 gives 70 columns on the 1125 px
wide presented panel, and the camera cannot resolve the hexadecimal digits
reliably, which blocks symbolication of user stacks.  At 4x the panel shows 35
columns x 38 rows with 32x64 px glyphs.

Base: pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c from CI main after 0109, saved as
tmp/pe_serial_after_0116.c.  Only pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c changes.
--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
@@ -715,7 +715,13 @@
 
 extern unsigned char iso_font[256 * 16];
 
-#define FBCON_SCALE     2
+/*
+ * onc: 4x instead of 2x.  The phone has no usable UART, so every kernel and
+ * userland console line is read off a 1080p camera photo; at 2x a 70-column
+ * line is at the edge of what the camera resolves.  At 4x the panel shows 35
+ * columns x 38 rows and the sampler/crash hex (pc/lr/bt) is readable.
+ */
+#define FBCON_SCALE     4
 #define FBCON_FG        0xffffffffu
 #define FBCON_BG        0xff000000u
 
